## 7. Cross-Instance Cache Invalidation (PostgreSQL NOTIFY)

When running multiple instances of the application, cache updates in one instance must trigger refreshes in others. This is achieved using PostgreSQL's `LISTEN/NOTIFY` mechanism.

### 7.1 Architecture

```
Instance A (writes)              PostgreSQL                Instance B (reads)
        │                            │                            │
        │── INSERT/UPDATE ──────────>│                            │
        │── NOTIFY channel ─────────>│                            │
        │                            │── notification ───────────>│
        │                            │                            │── TriggerRefresh()
```

### 7.2 Sending Notifications (Ops Thread)

After successful write operations, send a NOTIFY to alert other instances:

```go
// In {module}svc_ops.go (import "internal/cachenotify")

func notifyRefresh(db *database.PGSQLSvc) {
    ctx := context.Background()
    pool, err := db.GetDBInstance(ctx)
    if err != nil {
        return
    }
    _, _ = pool.Exec(ctx, "NOTIFY "+cachenotify.ChannelFoo)
}

func (o *FooSvc) opsHandleCreate(req *runMsgReq) {
    // ... DB write and commit ...

    // Notify OTHER instances first (they'll refresh from DB)
    notifyRefresh(o.db)

    // Then update local cache (optimization for this instance)
    rspCh := make(chan *runMsgRsp, 1)
    o.queryCh <- &runMsgReq{msgType: queryIntCacheAdd, msgData: &foo, rspCh: rspCh}
    <-rspCh

    req.rspCh <- &runMsgRsp{data: &foo}
}
```

### 7.3 Receiving Notifications (Listener)

A dedicated listener runs on a separate DB connection using `internal/cachenotify`:

```go
// internal/cachenotify/listen.go

// Channel names for PostgreSQL NOTIFY (single source of truth; use in switch in bootstrap).
const (
    ChannelTest    = "UPDATE_TEST_TABLE"
    ChannelAuth    = "UPDATE_AUTH_TABLE"
    ChannelAccount = "UPDATE_ACCOUNT_TABLE"
    // Add new channels here: ChannelFoo = "UPDATE_FOO_TABLE"
)

func Run(ctx context.Context, pgURL string, callback func(channel string), logger *log.Logger) {
    go run(ctx, pgURL, callback, logger)
}

func run(ctx context.Context, pgURL string, callback func(channel string), logger *log.Logger) {
    conn, err := pgx.Connect(ctx, pgURL)
    if err != nil {
        return
    }
    defer conn.Close(ctx)

    for _, ch := range []string{ChannelTest, ChannelAuth, ChannelAccount} {
        conn.Exec(ctx, "LISTEN "+ch)
    }

    for {
        notification, err := conn.WaitForNotification(ctx)
        if err != nil {
            return
        }
        callback(notification.Channel)
    }
}
```

Bootstrap (`cmd/main.go`) switches on the channel and calls each service's `TriggerRefresh()`:

```go
cachenotify.Run(context.Background(), *cfg.PgDB.PgURL, func(channel string) {
    switch channel {
    case cachenotify.ChannelAuth:
        authSvc.TriggerRefresh()
    case cachenotify.ChannelAccount:
        accountSvc.TriggerRefresh()
    case cachenotify.ChannelUser:
        userSvc.TriggerRefresh()
    case cachenotify.ChannelRole:
        roleSvc.TriggerRefresh()
    case cachenotify.ChannelMember, cachenotify.ChannelInvitation:
        // No in-memory cache to refresh (read-through DB)
    }
}, cacheLogger)
```

### 7.4 Service TriggerRefresh Method

Each service exposes a `TriggerRefresh()` method called by the listener:

```go
// In {module}svc.go

// TriggerRefresh reloads cache from DB (e.g. after NOTIFY from another instance).
func (o *FooSvc) TriggerRefresh() {
    if o.svcState.Load() != 1 {
        return
    }
    rspCh := make(chan *runMsgRsp, 1)
    select {
    case o.queryCh <- &runMsgReq{msgType: queryIntCacheRefresh, rspCh: rspCh}:
        <-rspCh
    default:
        // Channel full, skip (next periodic refresh will catch up)
    }
}
```

### 7.5 Adding a New Notify Channel

When creating a new module that needs cross-instance cache invalidation:

1. Add channel constant in `internal/cachenotify/listen.go`: `ChannelFoo = "UPDATE_FOO_TABLE"` (format: `UPDATE_<NAME>_TABLE`)
2. Add the constant to the LISTEN slice in `listen.go`
3. In the module's ops file: call `notifyRefresh()` after each write operation, using `cachenotify.ChannelFoo` in the NOTIFY (e.g. `pool.Exec(ctx, "NOTIFY "+cachenotify.ChannelFoo)`)
4. In application bootstrap: add a case in the cache-notify callback switch for `cachenotify.ChannelFoo` that calls the service's `TriggerRefresh()`

