## 16. Module Creation Checklist

When creating a new module:

- [ ] Create directory structure:
  - [ ] `internal/modules/{module}/{module}mdl/` - all models
  - [ ] `internal/modules/{module}/{module}svc/` - service layer
  - [ ] `internal/modules/{module}/{module}hdlr/` - HTTP handlers
- [ ] Define all models in `{module}mdl/`:
  - [ ] `{module}.go` - database entity model
  - [ ] `{module}_req.go` - request models (API input)
  - [ ] `{module}_rsp.go` - response models (API output)
  - [ ] `{module}_dto.go` - transformation functions
- [ ] Implement service with channel pattern:
  - [ ] `{module}svc.go` - struct, lifecycle, public API, `TriggerRefresh()` method
  - [ ] `{module}svc_ops.go` - write operations with `notifyRefresh()` calls
  - [ ] `{module}svc_query.go` - read operations with cache preload on startup
  - [ ] `{module}_cache.go` - cache implementation with `loadFromDB()` method
- [ ] Ensure cache preloads from DB before query thread processes requests
- [ ] If multi-instance cache sync needed:
  - [ ] Add channel in `internal/cachenotify/listen.go` (e.g. `ChannelFoo = "UPDATE_FOO_TABLE"`)
  - [ ] Call `notifyRefresh()` after write operations (use `cachenotify.ChannelFoo` for NOTIFY)
  - [ ] Wire callback case to service's `TriggerRefresh()` in bootstrap
- [ ] Implement handler with route registration
- [ ] Add schema to `resources/db/schema.sql`
- [ ] Update `docs/SCHEMA_DOC.md`
- [ ] Register routes in main router
- [ ] Start service in application bootstrap
- [ ] Add Swagger comments to each handler and run `go generate ./cmd` (see §18)

