## 18. API Documentation (Swagger)

The API is documented with **Swagger (OpenAPI 2.0)** via [swaggo/swag](https://github.com/swaggo/swag). The Swagger UI is served at `/swagger/` and lists all endpoints with request/response schemas.

### 18.1 Where Swagger Lives

| Item | Location |
|------|----------|
| API spec (generated) | `docs/docs.go`, `docs/swagger.json`, `docs/swagger.yaml` |
| General API info | `cmd/main.go` (comment block: `@title`, `@version`, `@host`, `@schemes`, `@BasePath`, `@securityDefinitions`) |
| Per-endpoint docs | Handler file that defines the route (e.g. `{module}hdlr/{module}hdlr.go`) |
| UI mount | `cmd/main.go`: `r.Mount("/swagger", httpSwagger.WrapHandler)` |

### 18.2 Documenting the API in Code

**Main application (cmd/main.go):** Define global API info and (optionally) health/system routes:

```go
//go:generate swag init -g main.go -o ../docs --parseDependency --parseInternal

// @title           WTTemplate API
// @version         1.0
// @description     Short description of the API.
// @BasePath        /
// @host            localhost:8080
// @schemes         http
// @securityDefinitions.apikey  BearerAuth
// @in                            header
// @name                          Authorization
package main
```

**Handlers:** Add swag comments **above** each handler function. Use the **full path** (including `/api/v1/...`) in `@Router`. Reference request/response types from the **module’s mdl package** (e.g. `authmdl.LoginReq`, `authmdl.LoginRsp`).

```go
// login authenticates user and returns token and user.
// @Summary  Login
// @Tags     auth
// @Accept   json
// @Produce  json
// @Param    body  body  authmdl.LoginReq  true  "Credentials"
// @Success  200   {object}  authmdl.LoginRsp
// @Router   /api/v1/auth/login [post]
func (h *AuthHdlr) login(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    // ...
}

// me returns the current user (requires JWT).
// @Summary  Current user
// @Tags     auth
// @Produce  json
// @Security BearerAuth
// @Success  200  {object}  authmdl.MeRsp
// @Router   /api/v1/auth/me [get]
func (h *AuthHdlr) me(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    // ...
}
```

**Rules:**
- Every public API endpoint MUST have a swag block: `@Summary`, `@Tags`, `@Router` at minimum.
- Use `@Param` for body/query/path; use `@Success`/`@Failure` with `{object} pkg.Type` for schemas.
- For JWT-protected routes add `@Security BearerAuth`.
- Keep `@Router` in sync with the actual route (e.g. `/api/v1/auth/login [post]`).

### 18.3 Regenerating Swagger Docs

After changing `@` comments in `cmd/main.go` or any handler:

```bash
# From repo root (requires swag on PATH)
go generate ./cmd
```

Or install and run swag explicitly:

```bash
go install github.com/swaggo/swag/cmd/swag@latest
swag init -g cmd/main.go -o docs --parseDependency --parseInternal
```

The generated `docs/` package is imported in `cmd/main.go` via `_ "github.com/albinzr/WTTemplate/docs"` so the spec is embedded at runtime.

### 18.4 Viewing and Using the API List

- **URL:** After starting the server, open `http://localhost:<port>/swagger/` (port from config `apiserver.port`).
- **Server URL in UI:** The `@host` and `@schemes` in the main block set the default server in Swagger UI (e.g. `http://localhost:8080`). “Try it out” uses this base URL.
- **Auth:** For endpoints with `@Security BearerAuth`, use the “Authorize” button and set the JWT (e.g. `Bearer <token>`).

### 18.5 Checklist for New or Changed Endpoints

- [ ] Added/updated swag comment block above the handler (Summary, Tags, Router, Param/Success where needed).
- [ ] Used full path in `@Router` (e.g. `/api/v1/auth/login [post]`).
- [ ] Referenced mdl types in `@Param`/`@Success`/`@Failure` (e.g. `authmdl.LoginReq`).
- [ ] Added `@Security BearerAuth` for JWT-protected routes.
- [ ] Ran `go generate ./cmd` and committed updated `docs/`.
